.el .ds Aq '
.TH taurctl 1  "taurctl 0.13.0" 
.SH NAME
taurctl \- Manage a TAUR server: accounts, packages, organizations and roles
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaurctl\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage a TAUR server: accounts, packages, organizations and roles
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Server URL (overrides TAUR_SERVER and the config file)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Config directory (default: $TAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print raw JSON
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin instead of prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
taurctl\-config(1)
Show or change CLI settings
.TP
taurctl\-register(1)
Create an account
.TP
taurctl\-login(1)
Sign in and store a session token (0600) in the config dir
.TP
taurctl\-logout(1)
End the session and delete the stored token
.TP
taurctl\-whoami(1)
Show the signed\-in account
.TP
taurctl\-unregister(1)
Delete your account (packages you maintain become orphans)
.TP
taurctl\-verify(1)
Confirm your email address with the token from the verification mail
.TP
taurctl\-resend\-verification(1)
Send the verification mail again
.TP
taurctl\-reset\-password(1)
Reset a forgotten password
.TP
taurctl\-search(1)
Search packages (AUR RPC)
.TP
taurctl\-info(1)
Show package details (AUR RPC)
.TP
taurctl\-org(1)
Manage organizations and member roles
.TP
taurctl\-pkg(1)
Manage package ownership
.TP
taurctl\-key(1)
Manage SSH public keys used for git pushes over SSH
.TP
taurctl\-comment(1)
Edit or delete package comments
.TP
taurctl\-request(1)
File and handle package requests (orphan, deletion, merge)
.TP
taurctl\-mcp(1)
Run an MCP server on stdio that forwards to the TAUR server\*(Aqs /mcp endpoint (uses the stored session token, if any)
.TP
taurctl\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Flags take precedence over environment variables.
.TP
\fBTAUR_SERVER\fR
TAUR server URL (overrides the config file).
.TP
\fBTAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR\fR
Config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl or ~/.config/taurctl).
.SH VERSION
v0.13.0
